# deploy-container.local.mk.example — machine-local deploy-container override
#
# TRACKED SOURCE lives in the operator's claude-config repo, NOT here:
#     claude-config/claude-container/deploy-container.local.mk
#         -> sets DEPLOY_DASHBOARDS_CMD to invoke the deploy-grafana-dashboards
#            target in the monitoring stack repo (andrew-sf-tools/monitoring),
#            which re-provisions the dashboards into the live Grafana.
#
# claude-watch's repo-root Makefile picks the override up via a conditional
# `-include` of the config-dir path:
#     ~/.config/claude-container/deploy-container.local.mk
# which is a SYMLINK to the tracked claude-config copy (same pattern as
# ~/.config/claude-container/mcp-host-bash.env). This keeps the override
# version-controlled + synced across hosts instead of a hand-made untracked file.
#
# ── Setup (idempotent) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/claude-container
#   ln -sfn ~/repos/claude-config/claude-container/deploy-container.local.mk \
#           ~/.config/claude-container/deploy-container.local.mk
#
# (This .example remains for a host WITHOUT claude-config: copy it to the config
#  dir as a plain file and uncomment a line below instead of symlinking.)
#
# ── What this configures ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `make deploy-container` folds FOUR things into one idempotent command:
#   1. force-recreate the claude-container service (the agent container);
#   2. redeploy the q-site / queue-minisite service (in this repo's compose);
#   3. deploy the Grafana dashboards LINKED IN from this repo
#      (monitoring/dashboards/{claude-watch,claude-events,work-queue}.json);
#   4. THIS override — the hook that lets #3 target an EXTERNAL, machine-specific
#      makefile/stack (andrew-sf-tools/monitoring) without editing the tracked Makefile.
#
# The canonical dashboard files live HERE in claude-watch, but the live Grafana
# that serves them (`monitoring-grafana-1`) is an EXTERNAL stack that bind-mounts
# those files and must be RESTARTED to re-provision (a provisioning-reload POST
# does NOT overwrite an already-provisioned dashboard).
#
# DEPLOY_DASHBOARDS_CMD must be:
#   * idempotent   — safe to re-run on every deploy;
#   * synchronous  — NO trailing `&` / nohup / disown (the deploy waits on it);
#   * self-contained — a single shell command line (use `$(MAKE) -f <file> <tgt>`
#                      to invoke an external makefile target).
#
# ── Examples (uncomment ONE) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# (a) PREFERRED: invoke the deploy-grafana-dashboards target in the monitoring
#     stack repo (andrew-sf-tools/monitoring), which restarts the local Grafana
#     container so it re-provisions from the linked-in dashboards (auto-discovers
#     the container by name; override GRAFANA_CONTAINER if the Grafana container
#     isn't named *grafana*):
#
# DEPLOY_DASHBOARDS_CMD = $(MAKE) -C $(HOME)/repos/andrew-sf-tools/monitoring deploy-grafana-dashboards
#
# (b) Minimal: just restart the live Grafana so it re-provisions from the
#     bind-mounted canonical dashboard files:
#
# DEPLOY_DASHBOARDS_CMD = docker restart monitoring-grafana-1
